/* Termination of a nested loop whose inner loop head is listed before the outer
   one, the order the TermCOMP ITS translation gives From_T2/bf10 and bsort100:
     i = 0;
     while (i < n) { j = 0; while (j < n) { j++; } i++; }
   Valid.  L11 is the outer loop head and L9 the inner one; the outer guard
   i < n sits on the call L11 -> L9 and the outer update i + 1 on the call
   L9 -> L11.  L11 is called only from predicates listed before it (L0 and L9)
   and does not call itself, so substituting its body for its occurrences is
   exact and leaves L9 calling itself directly, with the guard and the update
   on one call. */
forall (n: int). L0 n
s.t.
L0 (n: int): bool =mu L11 0 n;
L9 (i: int) (j: int) (n: int): bool =mu (j < n \/ L11 (i + 1) n) /\ (j >= n \/ L9 i (j + 1) n);
L11 (i: int) (n: int): bool =mu i >= n \/ L9 i 0 n;
